<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The process hinges on three pillars: daylight condition re‑inspection against pickup photos, odometer verification against the LR bilty, and a signed condition sign‑off.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Each step is documented and signed to protect both parties.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
<li><strong>Daylight Condition Re‑inspection</strong>
<ul>
<li>Inspect the vehicle under natural daylight to ensure no hidden damage.</li>
<li>Cross‑check the current exterior and interior condition with the high‑resolution pickup photos.</li>
<li>Document any discrepancies with photographs and a written note.</li>
<li>Confirm that all features (wipers, lights, mirrors) function correctly.</li>
</ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Odometer Verification</strong>
<ul>
<li>Read the odometer and compare the mileage to the figure listed on the LR bilty.</li>
<li>Verify that the vehicle’s mileage aligns with the service history and any prior records.</li>
<li>Record the verified mileage in the delivery log.</li>
<li>Flag any anomalies for further investigation.</li>
</ul>
</li>

<li><strong>Signed Condition Sign‑Off</strong>
<ul>
<li>Both the carrier and the recipient review the inspection report together.</li>
<li>Any noted issues must be agreed upon and documented.</li>
<li>Both parties sign the condition sheet, confirming acceptance of the vehicle’s state.</li>
<li>Attach the signed sheet to the final delivery paperwork.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>

<p>By adhering to this structured handover, the delivery team ensures transparency, reduces disputes, and upholds the integrity of the transaction. The final signed sign‑off becomes the official record that the vehicle was delivered in the agreed condition, providing peace of mind for the buyer and a clear audit trail for the carrier.</p></div>
